From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H96 build <builder@h96-build>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: re-add affected planes on
 output format change

On the no-modeset path a colour format change left planes with a stale
r2y CSC. dw_hdmi_connector_atomic_check() adds the CRTC's planes to
the state when the output state changed, so they redo their CSC.

H96 series: d2df7dee9 / e3b9f405e.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index a91ee8d38..a68419e76 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -3877,11 +3877,17 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_atomic_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
 
 	if (dw_hdmi_qp_state_changed(hdmi, connector, state) || hdmi->logo_plug_out) {
 		u32 mtmdsclk;
+		int ret;
 
 		crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(state, crtc);
 		if (IS_ERR(crtc_state))
 			return PTR_ERR(crtc_state);
 
+		/* planes redo their r2y csc for the new output format on the no-modeset path */
+		ret = drm_atomic_add_affected_planes(state, crtc);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
 		mtmdsclk = hdmi_get_tmdsclock(hdmi, mode.clock);
 		if (hdmi_bus_fmt_is_yuv420(hdmi->hdmi_data.enc_out_bus_format))
 			mtmdsclk /= 2;
